                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bbac00a0-cba8-3173-9c13-556dd5db4b77",
                        "entry_id": "26f1af83-cec8-35ba-8576-5ad04c032873",
                        "glosses": [
                            "met veel medegevoel"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f47fac0-f493-433d-a415-beb03a3612cd",
                                "sense_id": "bbac00a0-cba8-3173-9c13-556dd5db4b77",
                                "text": "Onze vakantiebestemming was Walcheren. Als je dat zegt, zie je sommige mensen een tikje medelijdend wegkijken, alsof je herinneringen wilt ophalen aan een vakantieoord voor kinderen uit achterstandswijken. „Toen ik in Bangkok overstapte naar Schiphol, had ik nog steeds heimwee naar Australië”, hoorde ik een vrouw deze week zuchten. Tegen zo iemand zeg je niet: „Zoutelande is ook aardig.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "440fa977-8365-401a-a8ae-c91a834139d5",
                                "sense_id": "bbac00a0-cba8-3173-9c13-556dd5db4b77",
                                "text": "„Wat deed ik verkeerd? Waarom laat Jeanine mij vallen?”, krijste hij vrijdagavond tegen zijn bevelhebbers. Zij keken hem medelijdend aan. Niets is erger dan een radeloze dictator zonder macht."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80b39cbe-7152-4312-bef6-3a459846a6bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "26f1af83-cec8-35ba-8576-5ad04c032873",
                        "source_sense_id": "bbac00a0-cba8-3173-9c13-556dd5db4b77",
                        "source_sense_description": "met veel medegevoel",
                        "target_lang_word": "compassionate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "compassionate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4175d86f-70f8-35b4-af0f-976ad34efb31",
                                        "entry_id": "9c9422e8-ae1c-3f9b-9e28-6ed9ac795525",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having, feeling or showing compassion (to or toward someone)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d8c9230-5201-4adf-8468-32ccc7ef8c9e",
                                                "sense_id": "4175d86f-70f8-35b4-af0f-976ad34efb31",
                                                "text": "The Compassionate, the All-Compassionate"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36fef498-f001-4b3f-a3e6-516ddcdd50de",
                                                "sense_id": "4175d86f-70f8-35b4-af0f-976ad34efb31",
                                                "text": "As a compassionate Turcoyse which doth tell\nBy looking pale, the wearer is not well,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca9a3900-97db-41f1-99cc-13c72677a5c3",
                                                "sense_id": "4175d86f-70f8-35b4-af0f-976ad34efb31",
                                                "text": "1675, Robert South, A Sermon preached at Christ-Church, in Twelve Sermons Preached upon Several Occasions, London: Thomas Bennett, 1692, p. 574,\n[…] there never was any heart truly great and generous, that was not also tender, and compassionate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "007c0815-745d-401e-be29-b6882e12cf77",
                                                "sense_id": "4175d86f-70f8-35b4-af0f-976ad34efb31",
                                                "text": "He was by nature so exceedingly compassionate of anyone who seemed to be ill at ease […] that he shook hands with Mr. Micawber, at least half-a-dozen times in five minutes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4da57f62-efb7-4f7d-82f8-b1548975629e",
                                                "sense_id": "4175d86f-70f8-35b4-af0f-976ad34efb31",
                                                "text": "[…] the compassionate pangs I felt for soon-to-be redundant workers were not overwhelming in their frequency; our job required a degree of commitment that left one with rather limited time for such distractions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "42dbb587-9d9e-3740-a816-afd417ee3278",
                                        "entry_id": "9c9422e8-ae1c-3f9b-9e28-6ed9ac795525",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Given to someone as an exception because of a family emergency or a death in their family."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbd8bd6c-32bc-408d-865f-9a6fdb340983",
                                                "sense_id": "42dbb587-9d9e-3740-a816-afd417ee3278",
                                                "text": "compassionate leave; a compassionate visa"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed093179-1e73-303a-adb0-3482766f0d2f",
                                        "entry_id": "9c9422e8-ae1c-3f9b-9e28-6ed9ac795525",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inviting or asking for pity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83b07892-2e66-4b2d-ae34-97b53599b796",
                                                "sense_id": "ed093179-1e73-303a-adb0-3482766f0d2f",
                                                "text": "It boots thee not to be compassionate:\nAfter our sentence plaining comes too late."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "compassionate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c580bab9-a2fc-3a11-8bf6-c77fd05e7ea1",
                                        "entry_id": "809b2810-bada-3e15-a65d-210e59411d7f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To feel compassion (for someone or with regard to something); to regard (someone or something) with compassion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36d1b54d-f20d-45b1-abf4-0f411dab741c",
                                                "sense_id": "c580bab9-a2fc-3a11-8bf6-c77fd05e7ea1",
                                                "text": "[…] seeing them die so wofully in the flames, he compassionated them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca5b3db7-07bd-437d-b544-a7e4975695d4",
                                                "sense_id": "c580bab9-a2fc-3a11-8bf6-c77fd05e7ea1",
                                                "text": "The Justice which Mr. Allworthy had executed on Partridge, at first met with universal Approbation; but no sooner had he felt its Consequences, than his Neighbours began to relent, and to compassionate his Case;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7e7a490-6e76-453b-94f9-e7e32a772009",
                                                "sense_id": "c580bab9-a2fc-3a11-8bf6-c77fd05e7ea1",
                                                "text": "And yet I could not help bitterly compassionating the honest fellow, brought to the gallows, as he was, strictly speaking, by the machinations of that devil incarnate, Mr. Tyrrel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2367eab7-7131-4b6f-9b25-9847fd3b2bc1",
                                                "sense_id": "c580bab9-a2fc-3a11-8bf6-c77fd05e7ea1",
                                                "text": "“[…] if she were a nice, pretty child, one might compassionate her forlornness; but one really cannot care for such a little toad as that.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e671519f-8ca8-4a8b-a84d-a814aa07ea6e",
                                                "sense_id": "c580bab9-a2fc-3a11-8bf6-c77fd05e7ea1",
                                                "text": "Helen laughed at these sentimental remarks, and wondered that Madame herself did not compassionate her lodger, and console him"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c53a855-ef7c-44fd-b24c-022c1b55d703",
                                                "sense_id": "c580bab9-a2fc-3a11-8bf6-c77fd05e7ea1",
                                                "text": "I explained the circumstances of the past two days, which had driven me to the woods, and he deeply compassionated my distress."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
